kwbackup (0.99.69) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat(vault): restore from the manifest chain

    kwbackup --restore --vault --to DIR [--at YYYY-MM-DD] [--from NAME] reads
    the manifests of the chosen target, keeps the newest base <= the date and
    applies the following layers; deleted paths are not extracted.

    A restore downloads each needed TAR volume once and extracts only the members
    present in the target state, then restores mode, uid/gid and mtime from the
    manifest. Restore order comes from vault.restore_order: direction desc/asc and
    top-level directory priority.

    Tests: latest restore with a deletion, --at against an older base, restore over
    the rsync transport, and a full rsync backup (80/80 e2e, 66 checks).

 -- Karel Wintersky <karel.wintersky@gmail.com>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:05:52 +0300

kwbackup (0.99.68) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat(vault): versioned file store (backup only)

    New task --vault: immutable TAR layers split by volume_size plus JSON
    manifests. The first run (--vault --full) scans the source and creates a base;
    daily runs consume the TXT journal (yesterday's file) or do a full scan when
    journal.type is scan. Every run creates a layer, even an empty one.

    Layers are named in UTC (YYYY-MM-DDTHHMMSSZ), manifests list
    added/modified/deleted and per-file volume/offset, and a unique-stamp check
    prevents one run from overwriting a layer created in the same second. A local
    sqlite index in state_dir speeds up the diff and is rebuilt from remote
    manifests if it is lost.

    Transports: upstreams gain type (rclone|rsync), bwlimit, host and ssh_options;
    non-rclone upstreams are accepted only for vault. TAR volumes hold whole files
    and are never compressed.

    --reconcile does a full scan without a new base; --full starts a new chain and
    marks the journals before the run as .done. restore/list/verify for vault are
    the next step.

    tests: full + empty layer, journal add/delete, reconcile, index rebuild, rsync
    transport, rsync upstream rejected for other tasks (78/78 e2e, 66 checks).

 -- Karel Wintersky <karel.wintersky@gmail.com>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:01:46 +0300

kwbackup (0.99.67) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat(journal): txt-daily journal reader for the vault task

    src/87_journal.py discovers <YYYY-MM-DD>.journal.txt files (only complete
    lines, the current day is skipped), parses "ts<TAB>op<TAB>path" records with
    validation (UTC timestamp, ADDED/MODIFIED/DELETED, relative path without ..),
    renames processed files to .done atomically, and removes .done files older
    than a TTL.

    The journal is only a hint: the future vault task will still stat-compare
    every path with the current chain, so duplicate, replayed or late records are
    harmless.

    No config or CLI yet - the vault task is the next step. The module is covered
    by the embedded selftest (64 checks, 72/72 e2e).
    TODO_VAULT.md records the deferred ideas: local transport, sqlite journal,
    physical prune and restore-order details.

