kwbackup (0.99.64) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat: honest --check, empty-source guard, database options

    --check now returns 1 when preflight finds problems (missing rclone or a
    dumper, unreadable sources, no space in temp_dir), logs them in one line and
    sends the failure notification when notify.on includes failure. Zero means
    everything is ready, so --check is usable from CI and monitoring.

    storage.allow_empty (false by default): sync refuses to run when a source
    directory is empty - the classic "the disk was not mounted" case that used to
    wipe the remote. copy is not affected and the flag lifts the guard.

    database.args now extends the built-in dump options instead of replacing
    them, so adding an option no longer drops --single-transaction. The new
    database.ignore_table list expands to --ignore-table=<db>.<table> for
    mysql/mariadb and --exclude-table=<table> for postgres; sqlite warns.

    Preflight checks cfg.rclone.binary for every action, including database
    dumps, which upload through rclone as well.

    Added examples/logrotate.d/kwbackup (log.file is opened per run, no signal
    needed); the example is shipped in the deb.

    tests: check exit code and notification, empty-source refusal and the
    allow_empty override, dump command assembly, ignore_table and allow_empty
    parsing (72/72 e2e, 57 checks).

