kwbackup (0.99.58) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat(config): disabled sections are parsed but not enforced

    A section with enabled: false used to be fully validated, so a stale upstream
    name or a half-written task broke every run, even --list and the action list.
    Now its errors are collected in Config.deferred_errors instead of being fatal:
    the action list marks the section "disabled, invalid config (see --check)" and
    --verbose logs each problem, but the other tasks keep working.

    --check still validates every section and exits 2. A run that would actually
    execute the section is strict as well: --force and --restore by that section.
    Errors in the enabled flag itself and in the root (project, upstreams, log,
    runtime) stay fatal.

    tests: disabled section is not enforced, bad enabled type is fatal, forced run
    is strict, selftest for load_config(strict=True) (57/57, 36 embedded checks).

