kwbackup (0.99.53) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat: incremental task (GNU tar chains)

    Fourth action, -i/--incremental. One chain per month, YYYY-MM embedded in the
    file names: <target>/<name>_<YYYY-MM>_full_<ts>.tar and ..._inc_<ts>.tar.

    A run belongs to the current month from initial_day (default 1, 1..28),
    otherwise to the previous month. The first run of a chain is a full dump
    (tar --level=0, which truncates the snapshot); later runs are increments via
    tar -g. A missing snapshot forces a full; restore picks the newest full in the
    chain. Retention (keep or max_age) deletes whole chains, never a lone
    increment. Plain .tar, no compression.

    Restore: --restore -i --to DIR [--from NAME] [--at YYYY-MM[-DD]] extracts the
    full and the increments in order with tar -x -g /dev/null; --at limits the
    layers to that date. --list shows chains, --verify checks the full and the
    last increment.

    config.incremental.snapshot is mandatory when enabled.

    tests: naming, changed files, chain retention, missing snapshot, restore
    chain, deleted file disappears, list/verify, --at (45/45).

