kwbackup (0.99.51) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat: multiple upstreams, one dump uploaded to every target

    New top-level `upstreams` map: key = the rclone remote name used in targets,
    value = {config, env, args, s3-custom-options}. `rclone` keeps only global
    settings; `rclone.remote` and `rclone.config` are gone.

    Sections take `targets: [upstream:path, ...]` instead of a single `target`.
    A dump or archive is produced once and uploaded to every target; retention
    prunes each target independently; a failing upstream is logged and the others
    still run (exit 1 at the end). `--list`/`--verify` walk all targets and
    `--from NAME` narrows them; `--restore --from NAME` picks the upstream.

    migrate emits the new shape; examples, docs and tests updated.

    tests: two upstreams with different configs, one broken upstream, restore
    --from, unknown upstream rejected (37/37).

