kwbackup (0.99.38) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat(config): typed rclone backend flags via s3-custom-options

    rclone accepts hundreds of backend flags; passing them as a list of
    '--s3-...' strings works, but a typed map is easier to override per action:

      rclone:
        s3-custom-options:
          s3-chunk-size: 5M
          s3-no-check-bucket: true
          s3-server-side-encryption: AES256

    Each entry becomes --<key>=<value>. Booleans render as --key (true) and
    --key=false (false); null removes an option inherited from rclone. Option
    names are not validated against a list, only their shape (no spaces, no
    leading dash). The same map is accepted in database, storage and archive,
    where it overrides rclone.s3-custom-options for that action only. The flags
    are appended after rclone.args, so the extended form wins.

    The simple path through rclone.args is unchanged.

    tests: global options, section override, boolean rendering, null removal,
    --check-config output (33/33).

 -- Karel Wintersky <karel.wintersky@gmail.com>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:40:26 +0300

