kwbackup (0.99.33) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat(config): drop the version field entirely

    The schema only grows, and an unknown key is already a hard error, so a
    schema version marker added nothing but a line of boilerplate in every task
    file. Removed from SECTIONS, from the validator, from the migrator output,
    from the examples and from the documentation.

    An old file that still carries 'version: 1' fails with a clear
    'config.version: unknown key' instead of being silently accepted.

 -- Karel Wintersky <karel.wintersky@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:58:47 +0300

kwbackup (0.99.32) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat(retention): prune only the files this config owns; archive name defaults to project

    Rotation used to delete every file with a parseable timestamp in the target
    directory. Two projects sharing an archive target - or two single-db configs
    sharing <target>/DAILY - deleted each other's copies.

    plan_prune takes a prefix now: <db>_ for dumps and <name>_ for archives.
    --list, --verify and --restore apply the same ownership filter, so a shared
    directory shows only what this config owns.

    archive.name no longer defaults to the literal 'archive': it defaults to the
    project name, which removes the project/name duplication from task files.
    Renaming it stops old files from being rotated, which is documented.

    tests: shared archive target, shared DAILY directory, default name (31/31).

