kwbackup (0.99.27) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat(logging): the terminal is quiet unless asked otherwise

    A backup run without flags used to print four INFO lines. In cron and
    systemd that is noise, and the useful information belongs in log.file.

      no flags   terminal: warnings and errors only; file: log.level
      --verbose  terminal: info; file: info; rclone --progress streams
      --debug    terminal and file: debug
      --dry-run  terminal: info (the plan is the output)

    'disabled in config' for an explicitly requested action is now a warning, so
    it stays visible in the quiet mode. Actions, --list, --verify, --check-config
    and migrate keep printing to stdout as before.

    tests: quiet default + info in the log file, verbose on the terminal,
    dry-run plan visible (27/27).

