kwbackup (0.99.26) unstable; urgency=medium

  * fix(rclone): stream rclone output under --verbose so --progress is visible

    rclone was always started with capture_output=True, so its progress and stats
    went into a captured stderr and were dropped unless the command failed. The
    --progress flag added in 0.99.25 was therefore invisible.

    run() now has capture=True/False. Rclone.run streams by default when VERBOSE
    is on and keeps capture for lsf, whose stdout must be parsed. A failed
    streamed command still reports the command and the exit code.

    tests: the fake rclone writes a progress line to stderr when --progress is
    present; it is hidden by default, visible with --verbose and --debug (26/26).

 -- Karel Wintersky <karel.wintersky@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:34:10 +0300

kwbackup (0.99.25) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat(cli): --verbose also makes rclone talk, --debug owns the debug log

    --verbose used to raise the script log to debug, which flooded the output,
    and it did not affect rclone at all. Now:

      --verbose  log stays at info, rclone gets --progress (stats + progress)
      --debug    log at debug (every command and its arguments), rclone --progress

    The rclone flag is added in Rclone._base(), so it applies to lsf, copyto,
    sync and deletefile alike. Neither flag changes behaviour, only output.

    tests: default run has no --progress and no command lines, --verbose adds
    --progress but keeps debug off, --debug adds both (26/26).

